   "evidence": "`coe_mapLinearMap` exists at Map/Basic.lean:118 with no counterpart for `mapFunctionLinearMap`. The diff replaces `ContMDiffSection.mapLinearMap_injective (fun x \u21a6 (D x).subtype) hD.contMDiff_totalSpace_inclusion fun _ \u21a6 Subtype.val_injective` with a manual pointwise proof.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/VectorBundle/Section/Map/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Add `theorem coe_mapFunctionLinearMap : (mapFunctionLinearMap \u03d5 h\u03d5 : C\u209b^n\u27eeI; F, V\u27ef \u2192 C\u209b^n\u27eeI; G, W\u27ef) = mapLinearMap \u03d5 h\u03d5 := (rfl)`. Then go back to the one-line `mapLinearMap_injective` proof of `toTangentSection_injective`.",
   "issue": "`mapFunctionLinearMap` has apply and `restrictScalars` lemmas but no coercion lemma. So `mapLinearMap_injective` can't be applied to it, and consumers have to evaluate pointwise. `Distribution/VectorBundle.lean:262-264` used `mapLinearMap_injective` before and now re-proves injectivity by hand (`ContMDiffSection.ext ... simpa using congr($h x)`).",
   "line": 194
  }
